                <pb facs="0907" n="779" xml:id="pg779"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 587.</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Valera to Mr. Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Spain at Washington</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-09-28"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 28,
                        1885</date>. (Received October 2.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>The undersigned, envoy extraordinary and minister plenipotentiary of his Majesty
                    the King of Spain, has the honor to inform the Hon. Thomas F. Bayard, Secretary
                    of State of the United States, that, as he is informed by the consul-general of
                    his nation at New York, the Cuban revolutionists are preparing to celebrate in
                    that city the anniversary of the outbreak of the insurrection of 1868, for which
                    purpose they have already appointed a committee of arrangements.</p>
                <p>The undersigned minister, in bringing this matter to the knowledge of the
                    honorable Secretary of State, does so solely in order that the administration
                    may be prepared to repress any expedition against the peace and tranquillity of
                    the island of Cuba that the insurrectionists may, perchance, desire to set on
                    foot as a concomitant to their aforesaid celebration.</p>
                <p>The undersigned, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JUAN VALERA.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
